---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import usage from '@/data/harness-usage.json'

const { buildPhase, session, providerPricing } = usage
const p = buildPhase.providerReported
const c = buildPhase.cost
const cacheHit = buildPhase.derived.cacheHitRatePercent
const whole = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-GB')
const compact = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-GB', {
  notation: 'compact', maximumFractionDigits: 2,
})
const percent = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(2)}%`
const usd = (value: number) => `US$${value.toFixed(2)}`
const rate = (value: number) => `US$${value.toLocaleString('en-GB', { maximumFractionDigits: 6 })}`
const share = (value: number) => p.totalTokens > 0 ? percent(value / p.totalTokens * 100) : '0.00%'
const elapsedMs = new Date(session.buildPhaseEndedAt).getTime() - new Date(session.startedAt).getTime()
const seconds = Math.round(elapsedMs / 1000)
const elapsed = Number.isFinite(seconds) && seconds >= 0
  ? `${Math.floor(seconds / 60)}m ${seconds % 60}s` : '—'
const ringPercent = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, cacheHit))
const costBarPercent = c.withoutCachingUsd > 0
  ? Math.max(0, Math.min(100, c.totalUsd / c.withoutCachingUsd * 100)) : 0
---

<Layout title="Building with DeepSeek Harness" description="Building an AI Token Cost Calculator with DeepSeek Harness: development, token usage, caching and subscription-based token valuations.">
<article id="harness-case-study">
  <div class="hr-wrap">
    <nav class="hr-top" aria-label="Project navigation"><a href="/projects/">← Back to Projects</a><span>29 October 2026</span></nav>
    <header class="hr-hero">
      <div class="hr-eyebrow">CASE STUDY · AI DEVELOPMENT</div>
      <h1>Building with<br>DeepSeek Harness</h1>
      <p class="hr-intro">Building an AI Token Cost Calculator and exploring the token usage, caching and development process behind it.</p>
      <p>DeepSeek Harness gives an AI model tools to inspect a project, edit files and run development commands. I used it to build a working calculator, then analysed the session records to understand how it used those resources.</p>
      <a class="hr-button" href="/projects/ai-token-calculator/">Explore the calculator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <section class="hr-finding" aria-labelledby="hr-finding-heading">
      <div>
        <div class="hr-eyebrow">THE BIG FINDING</div>
        <h2 id="hr-finding-heading">Almost all input came from cache</h2>
        <p>Across the recorded build phase, <strong>{percent(cacheHit)} of input tokens were cache reads</strong>. Previously processed context was reused across requests, rather than treated as entirely new input each time.</p>
        <p>This made caching the most interesting part of the session to investigate: a large token total could carry a much smaller value when most of the input was reused.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hr-ring" role="img" aria-label={`${percent(cacheHit)} of input tokens were cache reads`} style={`--hr-cache-hit:${ringPercent}%`}><div><strong>{percent(cacheHit)}</strong><span>input cache hit rate</span></div></div>
    </section>
    <dl class="hr-stats" aria-label="Recorded build-phase statistics">
      <div><dt>Cumulative tokens</dt><dd>{compact.format(p.totalTokens)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Elapsed build phase</dt><dd>{elapsed}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Model steps</dt><dd>{whole.format(buildPhase.steps)}</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <section class="hr-section" aria-labelledby="hr-token-heading">
      <div class="hr-eyebrow">UNDERSTANDING THE USAGE</div>
      <h2 id="hr-token-heading">Where the tokens went</h2>
      <p>Tokens are the small pieces of text processed by an AI model. The session records separate them into new input, cached input and generated output.</p>
      <div class="hr-table-wrap">
        <table class="hr-token-table">
          <caption>Build-phase token breakdown</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Token category</th><th scope="col">Tokens</th><th scope="col">Share of total</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Cached input<span>Previously processed context</span></th><td>{whole.format(p.cacheReadTokens)}</td><td>{share(p.cacheReadTokens)}</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">New input<span>Input processed without a cache read</span></th><td>{whole.format(p.uncachedInputTokens)}</td><td>{share(p.uncachedInputTokens)}</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Output<span>Text generated by the model</span></th><td>{whole.format(p.outputTokens)}</td><td>{share(p.outputTokens)}</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hr-section" aria-labelledby="hr-value-heading">
      <div class="hr-eyebrow">CACHING &amp; TOKEN VALUE</div>
      <h2 id="hr-value-heading">What does that usage represent?</h2>
      <p>I used a subscription allowance through OpenCode Go. To explore the effect of caching, I applied the model rates recorded in the project to the session’s token counts.</p>
      <p>That gives a token-rate valuation of approximately <strong>{usd(c.totalUsd)} with caching</strong>, compared with <strong>{usd(c.withoutCachingUsd)}</strong> if the cached input had been charged at the new-input rate. Output is held constant in both scenarios.</p>
      <figure class="hr-comparison" aria-label={`Token-rate valuation: ${usd(c.totalUsd)} with caching and ${usd(c.withoutCachingUsd)} without caching`}>
        <figcaption>Same workload, different input treatment</figcaption>
        <div class="hr-chart-row"><span>With caching</span><div class="hr-track"><div class="hr-bar" style={`width:${costBarPercent}%`}></div></div><strong>{usd(c.totalUsd)}</strong></div>
        <div class="hr-chart-row"><span>Without caching</span><div class="hr-track"><div class="hr-bar hr-bar-secondary" style="width:100%"></div></div><strong>{usd(c.withoutCachingUsd)}</strong></div>
        <div class="hr-chart-note">Illustrative valuation using recorded rates · both scenarios use the same output</div>
      </figure>
      <p>The comparison shows why the type of token matters as much as the total. A high cache-hit rate can substantially reduce a rate-based estimate.</p>
      <aside class="hr-note"><strong>Recorded rates</strong><p class="hr-rate-note">Per million tokens: {rate(providerPricing.input)} new input · {rate(providerPricing.cachedInput)} cached input · {rate(providerPricing.output)} output.</p></aside>
    </section>

    <section class="hr-section" aria-labelledby="hr-product-heading">
      <div class="hr-eyebrow">THE FINISHED PROJECT</div>
      <h2 id="hr-product-heading">A calculator for exploring AI costs</h2>
      <p>I wanted a clearer way to compare AI model pricing and see how changes in usage affect the result. The calculator separates new input, cached input and output, making the different charges easier to understand.</p>
      <p>Visitors can choose a model, enter token usage and adjust rates. The results show the cost breakdown and the effect of caching, with peak and off-peak comparisons where the pricing data supports them.</p>
      <figure class="hr-screenshot">
        <img class="hr-calculator-light" src="/images/projects/ai-token-calculator/calculator-desktop.webp" width="664" height="800" alt="AI Token Cost Calculator showing model selection, pricing and token inputs in light mode." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="hr-calculator-dark" src="/images/projects/ai-token-calculator/calculator-dark.webp" width="664" height="800" alt="AI Token Cost Calculator showing model selection, pricing and token inputs in dark mode." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>The finished calculator, showing model selection, pricing and token inputs.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="hr-build-detail"><h3>Pricing captured when the site is built</h3><p>The project uses Astro, a framework for building websites, with TypeScript for the calculator logic. Model pricing is retrieved from OpenRouter during the website build and included in the published page.</p><p>Calculations run in the visitor’s browser, so visitors need no API key and do not trigger a pricing request every time they use the tool. A saved pricing snapshot provides a fallback if the live request fails; the displayed rates reflect the latest successful refresh.</p></div>
      <a class="hr-text-link" href="/projects/ai-token-calculator/">Try the AI Token Cost Calculator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="hr-section" aria-labelledby="hr-process-heading">
      <div class="hr-eyebrow">THE DEVELOPMENT PROCESS</div>
      <h2 id="hr-process-heading">From brief to working application</h2>
      <p>My role was to set the requirements and review the completed result. The brief covered the calculator’s behaviour, its fit with my existing website and the checks I wanted performed. Harness carried out the implementation and recorded the development activity.</p>
      <ol class="hr-steps">
        <li><div class="hr-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</div><div><h3>Research and planning</h3><p>Harness inspected the existing Astro site and investigated OpenRouter’s model catalogue, including how to interpret its prices and conditional rates.</p></div></li>
        <li><div class="hr-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</div><div><h3>Building the calculator</h3><p>It implemented the calculation logic and interface, added editable rates and connected the build to a saved pricing fallback.</p></div></li>
        <li><div class="hr-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</div><div><h3>Checking and integration</h3><p>It ran calculation tests, browser checks and a production build, then integrated the calculator and initial case study into the project pages.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p>The development session used <strong>DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 through OpenCode Go</strong>. OpenRouter supplied the calculator’s pricing data. Keeping those roles separate is essential when interpreting the usage and valuation figures.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</article>
</Layout>
<style>
#harness-case-study {color-scheme:light;--hr-bg:light-dark(#ffffff,#18141f);--hr-ink:light-dark(#292331,#f4eff9);--hr-muted:light-dark(#615869,#c8becf);--hr-line:light-dark(#e7dfec,#403647);--hr-tint:light-dark(#f7f2fb,#272030);--hr-purple:light-dark(#70409c,#c5a4e7);--hr-quiet:light-dark(#b99bce,#79618e);background:var(--hr-bg);color:var(--hr-ink);font:15px/1.75 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;padding:34px 26px 56px;box-sizing:border-box}
#harness-case-study * {box-sizing:border-box}
#harness-case-study .hr-wrap {max-width:750px;margin:auto}
#harness-case-study h1,#harness-case-study h2,#harness-case-study h3,#harness-case-study p,#harness-case-study figure,#harness-case-study dl {margin:0}
#harness-case-study p {color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study p+p {margin-top:13px}
#harness-case-study p strong {color:var(--hr-ink);font-weight:650}
#harness-case-study a {color:var(--hr-purple);font-weight:650;text-decoration:none}
#harness-case-study a:hover {text-decoration:underline}
#harness-case-study .hr-top {display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:43px;font-size:13px;color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study .hr-eyebrow {color:var(--hr-purple);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.09em;font-weight:700}
#harness-case-study h1 {font-size:clamp(31px,5vw,46px);line-height:1.13;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:12px 0 18px}
#harness-case-study .hr-intro {font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--hr-ink);margin-bottom:17px;max-width:650px}
#harness-case-study .hr-hero>p:not(.hr-intro) {max-width:660px}
#harness-case-study .hr-button {display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:10px 15px;background:var(--hr-tint);border:1px solid var(--hr-line);border-radius:9px;font-size:14px;margin-top:22px}
#harness-case-study h2 {font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.25;margin:8px 0 15px}
#harness-case-study h3 {font-size:16px;line-height:1.4;margin-bottom:7px}
#harness-case-study .hr-finding {display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 165px;align-items:center;gap:30px;padding:28px;background:var(--hr-tint);border:1px solid var(--hr-line);border-radius:15px;margin-top:43px}
#harness-case-study .hr-ring {width:160px;height:160px;padding:12px;border-radius:50%;background:conic-gradient(var(--hr-purple) 0 var(--hr-cache-hit),var(--hr-line) var(--hr-cache-hit) 100%)}
#harness-case-study .hr-ring>div {height:100%;width:100%;border-radius:50%;background:var(--hr-tint);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:5px;text-align:center}
#harness-case-study .hr-ring strong {font-size:24px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:650;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
#harness-case-study .hr-ring span {font-size:12px;color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study .hr-stats {display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;margin-top:26px;padding:5px 0 0}
#harness-case-study .hr-stats dt {font-size:12px;color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study .hr-stats dd {font-size:23px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:3px 0 0;line-height:1.25;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
#harness-case-study .hr-caption {font-size:12px;margin-top:13px;line-height:1.65}
#harness-case-study .hr-section {display:flow-root;padding-top:40px;margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid var(--hr-line)}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table {width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:23px 0 0;font-size:13px;table-layout:fixed}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table caption {text-align:left;font-weight:650;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:8px}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table th,#harness-case-study .hr-token-table td {padding:12px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hr-line);vertical-align:top;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table th:first-child {width:49%;padding-left:0;text-align:left}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table thead th {font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table tbody th {font-weight:600}
#harness-case-study .hr-token-table th span {display:block;color:var(--hr-muted);font-size:12px;font-weight:400;margin-top:2px}
#harness-case-study .hr-comparison {padding:21px;margin:24px 0;background:var(--hr-tint);border-radius:12px}
#harness-case-study .hr-comparison figcaption {font-size:14px;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:15px}
#harness-case-study .hr-chart-row {display:grid;grid-template-columns:135px minmax(0,1fr) 75px;gap:13px;align-items:center;font-size:13px;margin:14px 0}
#harness-case-study .hr-chart-row strong {text-align:right;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
#harness-case-study .hr-track {height:12px;background:var(--hr-line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}
#harness-case-study .hr-bar {height:100%;background:var(--hr-purple);border-radius:12px}
#harness-case-study .hr-bar-secondary {background:var(--hr-quiet)}
#harness-case-study .hr-chart-note {color:var(--hr-muted);font-size:12px;padding-top:8px}
#harness-case-study .hr-note {margin:22px 0 0;padding:17px 20px;background:var(--hr-tint);border-left:3px solid var(--hr-purple);border-radius:0 9px 9px 0;font-size:14px}
#harness-case-study .hr-note>p {margin-top:7px}
#harness-case-study .hr-rate-note {font-size:12px}
#harness-case-study .hr-screenshot {margin:23px 0 27px}
#harness-case-study .hr-image-space {background:var(--hr-tint);border:1px dashed var(--hr-line);border-radius:12px;min-height:230px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:9px;text-align:center;padding:24px;color:var(--hr-muted)}
#harness-case-study .hr-image-space i {width:28px;height:28px}
#harness-case-study .hr-image-space strong {font-size:16px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hr-ink)}
#harness-case-study .hr-image-space span {font-size:13px}
#harness-case-study .hr-screenshot figcaption {font-size:12px;color:var(--hr-muted);margin-top:9px}
#harness-case-study .hr-build-detail {margin:20px 0 22px}
#harness-case-study .hr-steps {list-style:none;padding:0;margin:24px 0}
#harness-case-study .hr-steps li {display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px;padding:17px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hr-line)}
#harness-case-study .hr-step-number {font-size:12px;color:var(--hr-purple);font-weight:700;padding-top:2px}
#harness-case-study .hr-steps p {font-size:14px}
@media(max-width:560px){
  #harness-case-study {padding:25px 18px 40px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-finding {grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:23px;gap:23px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-ring {width:140px;height:140px;justify-self:center}
  #harness-case-study .hr-stats {gap:10px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-stats dt {font-size:12px;min-height:3.5em}
  #harness-case-study .hr-stats dd {font-size:20px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-token-table {font-size:13px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-token-table th,#harness-case-study .hr-token-table td {padding:11px 5px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-token-table th:first-child {width:43%}
  #harness-case-study .hr-token-table th:nth-child(2),#harness-case-study .hr-token-table td:nth-child(2) {width:34%;white-space:nowrap}
  #harness-case-study .hr-token-table th span {font-size:12px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-chart-row {grid-template-columns:1fr 74px;gap:7px}
  #harness-case-study .hr-chart-row>span {grid-column:1 / -1}
  #harness-case-study .hr-comparison {padding:18px}
}

:global(.dark) #harness-case-study {color-scheme:dark}
#harness-case-study .hr-screenshot img {display:block;width:100%;max-width:664px;height:auto;margin-inline:auto;border:1px solid var(--hr-line);border-radius:12px}
#harness-case-study .hr-screenshot .hr-calculator-dark {display:none}
:global(.dark) #harness-case-study .hr-screenshot .hr-calculator-light {display:none}
:global(.dark) #harness-case-study .hr-screenshot .hr-calculator-dark {display:block}
</style>
